The May '95 issue of Dr. Dobb's Journal has an article by yours truly on
the implementation of Linux kernel modules. Dr. Dobb's is a popular 
programming magazine published in the US, and this is their yearly 
issue on operating systems. It's the first main article in the magazine,
starting on page 18. It should be hitting the newsstands now.

The March '95 issue of DDJ awarded Linus Torvalds one of their annual 
"Excellence in Programming Awards" for the creation of Linux. DDJ is
one of the first "big" computer magazines to talk about Linux, and I hope 
that we'll see similar coverage from other journals in the future. You 
know, Linux is not just for breakfast anymore.

